        "id": 1181774
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-01T23:26:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we make sure this is cleared on CHIP_RESET?\n\nAlso, cleared if there is a disconnect before the event is cleared by the AP?\n\n\nThe way this would be parse by the AP is :\n1. AP calls TYPEC_STATUS\n2. If AP sees HARD_RESET it does the following:\n  a. send a uevent to let userspace know a hard reset happened.\n  b. unregister the partner \u0026 cable.\n\nI don\u0027t know if we should additionaly do c.) \"re-register partner and cable\" while handling this event itself, or will another PD event come soon after the hard_reset event (and the re-registration can happen then).",
      "revId": "7d6270a49176d58671d7742a1013711bd26e5d90",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c118bf4a_4d167e67",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-02T16:45:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done.\n\nIf things are working normally, there should be a discovery event later that you could re-register on. In the meantime, I think there will be at least one PD_MCU event for VBUS toggling during the Hard Reset, but there won\u0027t be valid discovery info during this interval. If you query discovery info immediately upon the Hard Reset event, we might have to worry about a race between that and the EC clearing the discovery info.",
      "parentUuid": "6c974ada_49b06a21",
      "revId": "7d6270a49176d58671d7742a1013711bd26e5d90",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1faac87f_421260a9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1181774
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-02T18:59:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  If you query discovery info immediately upon the Hard Reset event, we might have to worry about a race between that and the EC clearing the discovery info.\n\nThanks for the context. So, the potential issue I see is that by the time the kernel gets around to handling the Hard Reset-PD MCU event, re-discovery might already be complete. Since all these events are returned by the same TYPEC_STATUS host command, we may get into a situation where all the all three events are set.\n\nSo, we should figure out what\u0027s the appropriate way to handle the hard reset event. Is it:\n1. De-register partner and cable, and then exit (and let subsequent events re-register things) regardless of what the SOP_DISC_DONE and SOP_PRIME_DISC_DONE event bits show.\n2. De-register partner and cable, and then if *_DISC_DONE are also set, try re-registering?\n\nPer your comment 2.) might be racy, so if we\u0027re confident that another event is going to come in soon after, we should go with 1.)\n\n\nAlso, will the event be cleared when a physical disconnect occurs (Unattached.*) ?",
      "parentUuid": "c118bf4a_4d167e67",
      "revId": "7d6270a49176d58671d7742a1013711bd26e5d90",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6961b61f_96cafbd7",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-02T19:59:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Also, will the event be cleared when a physical disconnect occurs (Unattached.*) ?\nNot right now, but it probably should be.\n\n\u003e So, we should figure out what\u0027s the appropriate way to handle the hard reset event. Is it:\n\u003e 1. De-register partner and cable, and then exit (and let subsequent events re-register things) regardless of what the SOP_DISC_DONE and SOP_PRIME_DISC_DONE event bits show.\n\u003e 2. De-register partner and cable, and then if *_DISC_DONE are also set, try re-registering?\nI think what you\u0027re pointing out is that, if both bits are set, the correct interpretation depends on which one was set first (which you can\u0027t know as of this patchset). If discovery done was set first, then you should ignore it, unregister, and wait for another discovery done. If HR was set first, you should unregister and reregister.\n\nI believe I can avoid the issue by clearing the discovery flags before setting the HR flag. That way, if you see both, you\u0027ll know that the HR flag came first.\n\nDiana: Does my proposal sound like a maintenance hazard to you? Can you think of a more elegant way to handle this?",
      "parentUuid": "1faac87f_421260a9",
      "revId": "7d6270a49176d58671d7742a1013711bd26e5d90",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
